("premiere",None,"Madama Butterfly premiered at La Scala on 17 February 1904 in a two-act version, and was withdrawn after a disastrous first night.",["had its premiere on 17 February 1904 at La Scala in Milan","was withdrawn after a disastrous premiere"]),
("blooper",None,"At the 1904 premiere, audience plants were given nightingale whistles for the sunrise. The audience took it as a cue to make animal noises of their own.",["give audience plants nightingale whistles to deepen the sense of sunrise in the final scene","The audience took the noise as a cue to make their own animal noises."],"Reception"),
("premiere",None,"The premiere was called \u201cone of the most terrible flops in the history of Italian opera\u201d. One problem: no intermission in the very long second act.",["one of the most terrible flops in the history of Italian opera","the lack of an intermission during the second act"],"Reception"),
("composer",None,"Puccini\u2019s sister Ramelde wrote that night: \u201cThe second act I didn\u2019t hear at all, and before the opera was over, we ran out of the theater.\u201d","The second act I didn't hear at all, and before the opera was over, we ran out of the theater.","Reception","Ramelde Puccini, letter to her husband, 1904 (via Wikipedia)"),
("history",None,"Puccini rewrote it, splitting the long second act in two. The new version was a great success in Brescia on 28 May 1904.",["splitting the second act in two","This second version (SC 74.B) was performed on 28 May 1904 in Brescia, where it was a great success"]),
("music","Humming|Coro a bocca chiusa|bocca chiusa","The Humming Chorus became the bridge between Puccini\u2019s new Acts II and III.","with the Humming Chorus as a bridge to what became Act III"),
