("history",None,"Butterfly reached the Metropolitan Opera on 11 February 1907, in Puccini\u2019s third version.","which was performed at the Metropolitan Opera in New York on 11 February 1907","Versions"),
("history",None,"The first US performances, in 1906, were in English, by Henry Savage\u2019s touring company.","the first US performance was presented in English on 15 October 1906, in Washington, D.C.","Performance_history"),
("music","Bimba dagli occhi|Vogliatemi bene","From the long love duet that closes Act I: \u201cBimba dagli occhi pieni di malia\u201d, \u201cSweetheart, with eyes full of enchantment\u201d.","Bimba dagli occhi pieni di malia (\"Sweetheart, with eyes full of enchantment\")","Act_1"),
("music","Ora a noi|Sharpless|lettera","Sharpless brings a letter from Pinkerton asking him to break the news that he isn\u2019t coming back to Japan.","Pinkerton is not coming back to Japan","Act_2"),
("music","Il cannone|Scuoti quella fronda","\u201cIl cannone del porto!\u201d, the cannon at the harbor, leads into the famous Flower Duet.","Il cannone del porto! (\"The cannon at the harbor!\", often known as The Flower Duet).","Act_2"),
("history",None,"The musical Miss Saigon (1989) was inspired by Madama Butterfly.","Miss Saigon, a musical by Claude-Michel Schönberg and Alain Boublil, is inspired by the opera","Adaptations"),
